 .TP
-.B VLC_DATA_PATH
-The directory containing VLC run-time data files (e.g. /usr/share/vlc).
-
+.B http://example.com/stream.m3u8
+HTTP stream (including HLS)
 .TP
-.B VLC_PLUGIN_PATH
-An extra directory to load VLC plugins from.
-
+.B rtsp://server:554/stream
+RTSP stream
+.SH KEYBOARD CONTROLS
+The following are the default keybindings on Linux (X11/Wayland). They can
+be changed in
+.B Preferences > Hotkeys.
+.PP
+.TS
+l l.
+Key(s)	Action
+_
+Space	Play/Pause
+f	Toggle fullscreen
+Esc	Leave fullscreen
+n	Next item in playlist
+p	Previous item in playlist
+s	Stop
+Ctrl+q	Quit VLC
+Ctrl+Up	Volume up
+Ctrl+Down	Volume down
+m	Mute/Unmute
+l	Loop playlist
+r	Random (shuffle)
+t	Show current position
+a	Cycle aspect ratio
+c	Cycle crop
+d	Toggle deinterlace
+Shift+d	Cycle deinterlace mode
+v	Cycle subtitle track
+Shift+v	Toggle subtitles
+b	Cycle audio track
+Shift+s	Take snapshot
+Shift+r	Start/Stop recording
+i	Show/hide interface
+Ctrl+Left	Short jump backward (10s)
+Ctrl+Right	Short jump forward (10s)
+Alt+Left	Medium jump backward (1m)
+Alt+Right	Medium jump forward (1m)
+Shift+Left	Extra short jump backward (3s)
+Shift+Right	Extra short jump forward (3s)
+h/g	Subtitle delay up/down
+k/j	Audio delay up/down
+z	Zoom in
+Shift+z	Zoom out
+o	Toggle autoscale
+w	Toggle wallpaper mode (where supported)
+Shift+m	Disc menu
+Shift+o/b	Title previous/next
+Shift+p/n	Chapter previous/next
+Page Up	Increase 360° field of view
+Page Down	Decrease 360° field of view
+F1..F10	Play bookmark 1..10
+Ctrl+F1..F10	Set bookmark 1..10
+Ctrl+w	Clear playlist
+.TE
+.PP
+Many more actions exist (subtitles delay, audio delay, recording, rate control,
+bookmarks, etc.). See the Hotkeys preferences panel for the complete list
+and to customize bindings.
+.SH MOUSE CONTROLS
+.TP
+.B Left click
+Pause/resume playback (configurable).
+.TP
+.B Double left click
+Toggle fullscreen.
+.TP
+.B Right click
+Open the popup/context menu.
+.TP
+.B Middle click
+Often toggles mute or performs a configurable action.
+.TP
+.B Mouse wheel (vertical)
+Volume control by default (see
+.B hotkeys-y-wheel-mode
+option). Can be set to seek position or ignored.
+.TP
+.B Mouse wheel (horizontal)
+Seek/position control by default (see
+.B hotkeys-x-wheel-mode
+option).
+.PP
+.SH MOUSE GESTURES
+The "gestures" module (enabled via interface selection or preferences) allows
+controlling VLC using mouse movements while holding a mouse button (usually
+right button). Common gestures include:
+.TP
+.B Left/right
+Seek backward/forward.
+.TP
+.B Up/down
+Volume up/down.
+.TP
+.B Other shapes
+Play/pause, fullscreen, stop, etc. (fully configurable).
+.PP
+Gestures can be enabled in the interface settings.
+.SH LISTING AND CUSTOMIZING CONTROLS
+To view or change all current keybindings and mouse actions:
+.IP \(bu
+Open VLC and go to
+.B Tools > Preferences > Hotkeys.
+This shows every action with its current binding.
+.IP \(bu
+Mouse wheel behavior is configured under
+.B Interface > Mouse wheel.
+.IP \(bu
+From the command line you can inspect the active configuration with
+.B vlc \-\-list
+or by examining the configuration file (usually
+.I ~/.config/vlc/vlcrc
+or
+.I ~/.vlc/vlcrc
+on older systems) after using the GUI to view settings.
+.PP
+All controls are stored in the configuration and can be overridden on the
+command line or in the config file.
+.SH INTERFACES
+.TP
+.B cvlc
+Command-line interface (no GUI).
+.TP
+.B nvlc
+NCurses (console) interface.
+.TP
+.B rvlc
+Remote control interface.
+.TP
+.B qvlc / svlc
+Qt / Skins interfaces (default on most desktops).
+.SH ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
+See the full list with
+.B vlc \-\-help
+or in the source. Common ones include:
 .TP
 .B VLC_VERBOSE
-The level of verbosity for log messages
-(0: silent, 1: error/info, 2: warning, 3: debug).
-
-.TP
-.B XDG_CACHE_DIR XDG_CONFIG_DIR XDG_DATA_DIR
-The directories to store user cached data, user configuration files and
-user data files respectively.
-
-.TP
-.B XDG_DOCUMENTS_DIR XDG_DOWNLOAD_DIR XDG_MUSIC_DIR XDG_PICTURES_DIR XDG_VIDEO_DIR
-The directories to fetch or store user text files,
-downloads, music, pictures (i.e. snapshots), and video respectively.
-
-.TP
-.B XDG_SESSION_COOKIE
-The unique identifier of the desktop session,
-used by the PulseAudio output plugin.
-
+Verbosity level (0-3).
+.TP
+.B VLC_PLUGIN_PATH
+Additional plugin search path.
+.TP
+.B DISPLAY
+X11 display (when relevant).
+.TP
+.B VLC_DATA_PATH
+Directory containing runtime data files.
